================================================================================
THIRD-PARTY NOTICE
================================================================================

This project is an unaffiliated, independent tribute to Omarchy, and is not
endorsed by or affiliated with its authors.

Omarchy
  https://omarchy.org
  https://github.com/omacom/omarchy
  Copyright (c) David Heinemeier Hansson (DHH) and contributors
  Licensed under the MIT License.

  This project reproduces Omarchy's *behaviour and design* — its menu tree,
  keyboard bindings, bar layout and module order — and transcribes its theme
  colour palettes (themes/<name>/colors.toml on branch `quattro`) so that the
  reconstruction is colour-accurate. No Omarchy source code, binary, ISO or
  photographic asset is included or redistributed here. All wallpapers and
  artwork in this project are generated procedurally at runtime from the active
  colour palette.

Hyprland — https://hypr.land — the tiling compositor whose semantics the
  window-management engine in src/wm.js imitates. Not redistributed.

Quickshell — https://quickshell.org — the shell toolkit Omarchy 4 is built on.
  Not redistributed.

Theme palettes are derived from the upstream Omarchy theme definitions, which
in turn draw on the following community colour schemes, each the work of its
own authors: Tokyo Night, Catppuccin, Ethereal, Everforest, Flexoki, Gruvbox,
Kanagawa, Nord, Rosé Pine, Ristretto, Osaka Jade, and others. See
src/themes.js for the full list of 23 palettes.
